  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A pressed cake of lantern bract ground with water and a mat binder, ultraviolet-bright and, to a human eye, a dull pinkish grey. Bracts are collected in the canopy, dried for a season, ground between two shells and pressed in a ring mould; a cake this size is about four hundred bracts and a fortnight of somebody&#39;s evenings. It was ground in front of the 2270 team, which is why the date is exact, and half of it was used the same day to mark a span boundary. What remains has faded under storage lighting and no longer reads correctly under a filter, a fact the conservation file records twice and explains once.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
